  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="A Matrix Reveals Its Favorite Directions" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Both panels use the same Cartesian units. Left: input circle. Right: the staged image and a fixed target outline.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.4249999999999998,0.0,0.04249999999999999],\&quot;size\&quot;:[10.285,6.159999999999999,0.745]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;dfa81e424e9fcd3fa71186f5b4785d567c540358c6a077164eb9e90fac061527\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;Left and right panels use equal Cartesian scale, with x translations −3 and +2.3. Subtract the appropriate panel center before comparing vector coordinates.\&quot;,\&quot;Only progress=3 displays the target A. The target singular values and violet outline stay fixed during the instructional path; the displayed determinant belongs to the current staged map.\&quot;,\&quot;This family chooses rotations U,V and sorted nonnegative stretches. General real matrices may require orthogonal reflections as well; an arbitrary determinant-negative matrix is not covered by these controls.\&quot;,\&quot;At σ₂=0 the target is rank one and cannot be inverted; no finite condition number is reported. If σ₁=σ₂, the choice of singular directions is not unique.\&quot;,\&quot;The checks compare matrix multiplication, rank-one reconstruction and Avⱼ=σⱼuⱼ. Small floating-point residuals check implementation consistency rather than prove the general SVD theorem.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;svd\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;stage\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Currently displayed stage\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:\&quot;complete target A\&quot;},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;display_area\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Displayed signed-area factor\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Determinant of the current staged matrix, not automatically that of target A.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;×\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.4},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;sigma1\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Target σ₁\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:2},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;sigma2\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Target σ₂\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.7},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;condition\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Target condition number κ₂(A)\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Singular values describe the target; only progress=3 shows that complete target.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:2.857142857142857},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;direction_residual\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Target max ||Avⱼ−σⱼuⱼ||\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:5.551115123125783e-17}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;angle_u\&quot;:0.65,\&quot;angle_v\&quot;:-0.45,\&quot;progress\&quot;:3,\&quot;ratio\&quot;:0.35,\&quot;sigma1\&quot;:2},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;29a8017c26c30494c4cadd54a60c97790e2f6bad7f4d11107e6292cd61a0bc68\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;A Matrix Reveals Its Favorite Directions\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
